{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore","id":1482292,"title":"Demons in VTM lore vs Demons in DTF lore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-29T15:03:47-07:00","id":1482292,"title":"Demons in VTM lore vs Demons in DTF lore","content":"Demons in VTM lore are shown to be extremely cruel and powerful beings with extremely strange and terrifying powers that would make any vampire scream and run to their sires.<br /> <br /> However in DTF lore, demons are perhaps the weakest supernatural's to walk the earth. Their powers, known as lore's, are either discount disciplines, or knock off blood magic paths. I am not joking when I say that you could put an earthbound up against an old clan tzimisce elder, and expect to see the elder teabag the earthbound while its cultists start running from the elders ghouls.<br /> <br /> Compared to the disciplines that vampires posses, the lore's of the fallen are pretty pathetic. Now don't get me wrong, when I mean pathetic, I mean pathetic for a demon, a fallen angel that has been around since the beginning. The lore's feel better suited for a vampire than creatures like them.<br /> <br /> How about we talk a bit about cultists, let me remind you all that the earthbounds who have powerful cults honestly lucked out, you could look through the wiki page of most earthbounds and see that while the earthbound went to sleep for centuries, their cultists were able to grow strong without any of their help. Unlike vampire elders that either built or took control of a company/industry by the sheer power of their ambition and confidence, and now control a good portion of a country's government. In other words, a vampire elder is probably better than any demon when it come to leadership.<br /> <br /> And honestly, what can the fallen give you anyway that a vampire cant? I can assure you that a vampire can give you anything a fallen can, maybe even better.<br /> <br /> Lets not forget that regular fallen need a human host or else they are screwed. This means all you need is a mortal with a gun/knife/baseball bat/anything that can be used as a weapon, and you have technically slayed a demon.<br /> <br /> Oh and blood is easier to get than faith, case closed.<br /> <br /> *In all honesty Kupala should not have been an earthbound, he should have been some powerful nature spirit, because looking at the powers an earthbound posseses, it makes no sense why the eldest would have formed an alliance with him.<br /> <br /> *I know that vampires who serve demons are supposed to be hated by the rest, but if you're going to serve a fallen from the DTF, I feel like you're more likely to be laughed at. So it makes more sense that the baali serve creatures like neverborn or banes.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, so correct me if I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-29-2022, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:21:04-07:00","id":1482312,"title":"","content":"The demons of V:tM aren't the Fallen, and don't have the Fallen's limitations, because the demons of V:tM aren't designed like player characters. It's tempting to mistake NPC lore for player character game mechanics, and this happens with Vampire's Methusaleh NPC's doing impossible things in lore and fiction too.<br /> <br /> The Fallen do have tricks of their own up their sleeve, though. Lore of the Fundament is the best of Celerity and Potence, with some extra powers like wall-crawling on the side. If you can grapple somebody and throw them nine stories up into the air, and they don't have wings, you've killed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:33:35-07:00","id":1482313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482312#post1482312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The demons of V:tM aren't the Fallen, and don't have the Fallen's limitations, because the demons of V:tM aren't designed like player characters. It's tempting to mistake NPC lore for player character game mechanics, and this happens with Vampire's Methusaleh NPC's doing impossible things in lore and fiction too.<br /> <br /> The Fallen do have tricks of their own up their sleeve, though. Lore of the Fundament is the best of Celerity and Potence, with some extra powers like wall-crawling on the side. If you can grapple somebody and throw them nine stories up into the air, and they don't have wings, you've killed them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:47:50-07:00","id":1482314,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that DTF demons aren't the only kind of demons in WoD, High-umbral spirits capable of anything that fits their concept(MtA), Malevolent Nature Spirits known as Banes(WtA), Thallian changelings and Dark Fae in the Deep Dreaming(CtD), Ancient Spectres and infernal Malpheans(WtO), Servants of Apophis(MtR), Yama Kings and their Akuma(KotE), and Other Stranger things.<br /> <br /> Everything mentioned above has one or more &quot;demonic deal&quot; abilities in their mechanics. All of that roaming around with the uncomfortable realization that there's very little way for any vampire to tell the difference between any of the above without methusela levels of occult and demonology knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:53:25-07:00","id":1482316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482314#post1482314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that DTF demons aren't the only kind of demons in WoD, High-umbral spirits capable of anything that fits their concept(MtA), Malevolent Nature Spirits known as Banes(WtA), Thallian changelings and Dark Fae in the Deep Dreaming(CtD), Ancient Spectres and infernal Malpheans(WtO), Servants of Apophis(MtR), Yama Kings and their Akuma(KotE), and Other Stranger things.<br /> <br /> Everything mentioned above has one or more &quot;demonic deal&quot; abilities in their mechanics. All of that roaming around with the uncomfortable realization that there's very little way for any vampire to tell the difference between any of the above without methusela levels of occult and demonology knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you think the WOD couldnt get any more darker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:53:49-07:00","id":1482317,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when you look at stuff like Yama Kings and their servants, those are the sort of things that vampires would make alliances to or become subservient to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T18:55:36-07:00","id":1482318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482316#post1482316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you think the WOD couldnt get any more darker.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL yeah, there's always something in the dark for the playable monsters to be afraid of!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:11:44-07:00","id":1482326,"title":"","content":"While I completely agree that the &quot;demons&quot; VtM talks about usually aren't Fallen, but any number of other beings, I think the arguments on the Fallen in the OP are at best simplistic.<br /> <br /> Comparing Lores to Disciplines isn't an objective thing because Demon never had a Second edition and was published in a tight schedule, so their design suffers a lot. Even then they're a mixed bag, some are weak, some are pretty strong, and in general they have pretty easy access to even their most obscene powers in comparison to other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And outside that, their Innate Powers combined are what makes the Fallen extremely dangerous if they're cunning. They can perceive supernatural powers from miles of distance, ignore the most common non-physical effects that could hinder them and with a very basic setup for a Demon they can come back from the dead freely in a new body. Combat will depend a lot on the details of a given Apocalyptic Form.<br /> <br /> Lores usually have no upper limit on how much the effect improves with successes, and the Fallen can use their Thralls to gather huge amounts of dice easily. Faith also definitely isn't harder to get than blood: each Thrall you make gives you Faith every day for as long as the Thrall survives, regardless of distance or anything else. Getting enough Thralls to fill completely every day isn't hard, and you can go further and travel the globe once in a while to setup so you collect Faith several times a day.<br /> <br /> If we talk about Infernalism and Pacts, though, most of this is irrelevant. Vampires summon entities they can't comprehend to bargain their souls. Those entities don't need to be specially strong, they need to convince the vampire, and to be able to pull off the Pact. Fallen are perfectly capable of doing that. In the context of a Pact they get a lot of leeway outside their usual power range based on the Faith Potential of the future Thrall, most boons described can be accomplished with relative ease in this setup. On top of that the Fallen gets permanent attachment to the Thrall that can be used in several ways, <i>including draining Willpower and Health to death with just a thought and with no resistance whatsoever</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T22:04:19-07:00","id":1482347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482326#post1482326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we talk about Infernalism and Pacts, though, most of this is irrelevant. Vampires summon entities they can't comprehend to bargain their souls. Those entities don't need to be specially strong, they need to convince the vampire, and to be able to pull off the Pact. Fallen are perfectly capable of doing that. In the context of a Pact they get a lot of leeway outside their usual power range based on the Faith Potential of the future Thrall, most boons described can be accomplished with relative ease in this setup. On top of that the Fallen gets permanent attachment to the Thrall that can be used in several ways, <i>including draining Willpower and Health to death with just a thought and with no resistance whatsoever</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side-note though: Human-bodied fallen and Recently summoned DTF demons can't make deals with vampires at all, because they don't Have a faith potential in the way a fallen would understand it(no faith potential score). The only DTF entities that can side-step this are earthbound, because they don't actually use up their thralls faith potential in pacts and instead contaminate a pact bearer with the Earthbound's Own essence(Pact bearer turns 1 dot of permanent willpower into 15 freebies with even more options instead of 1 faith potential into 10). Good news: This means they can't be ravaged as well because Earthbound can't Do that.<br /> <br /> Bad news: the typical &quot;Deal&quot; as a vampire would envision would come from corrupt pseudo-gods who can End your capacity for free will if you make too many pacts with them and can use their &quot;mastery&quot; background to amp their lore abilities to Biblical levels if you piss them off. Don't do infernalism Kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T23:06:44-07:00","id":1482350,"title":"","content":"A reminder that Demons in Demon: The Fallen are dramatically weakened because they're wearing human suits and are the smallest to escape through the cracks.<br /> <br /> Also, the lores are RIDICULOUSLY OP once you're out of a human suit.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Level 5: Destroy California.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T04:09:00-07:00","id":1482364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482350#post1482350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reminder that Demons in Demon: The Fallen are dramatically weakened because they're wearing human suits and are the smallest to escape through the cracks.<br /> <br /> Also, the lores are RIDICULOUSLY OP once you're out of a human suit.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Level 5: Destroy California.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesent that require a lot of faith though? If I remember properly, the wiki pointed out that one of the archdukes used up a large amount of the faith they collected just to send an earthquake across LA, and it wasn't even a state. Most earthbound probably cant even do that, and most fallen that aren't earth bound cant do what an earthbound is capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T06:57:38-07:00","id":1482370,"title":"","content":"In a straight fight, Demons typically lose to a Vampire with similar xp, that's true. About the only thing that comes close to putting them on equal footing is the optional rule to buy new Apocalyptic Form abilities. And, you know, the daylight thing. <br /> <br /> I will say, some of the Lores are quite nice for taking out Vampires though. Lore of Flame immediately come to mind, especially if you treat Blood Points as Faith Points for the purposes of Lore of Flame's Holocaust ability (I personally do) and access to Ride the Flame is pretty much the &quot;I Win&quot; Button against Vampires. <br /> <br /> Oh, and the power level between Fallen and Earthbound isn't even on the same scale. A maxed out Earthbound is probably the strongest supernatural on Earth. I'd put &quot;the five&quot; above even the Antediluvians in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T08:29:37-07:00","id":1482373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482364#post1482364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesent that require a lot of faith though? If I remember properly, the wiki pointed out that one of the archdukes used up a large amount of the faith they collected just to send an earthquake across LA, and it wasn't even a state. Most earthbound probably cant even do that, and most fallen that aren't earth bound cant do what an earthbound is capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>It honestly depends on the Earthbound's Lores and how high their mastery background is. The Earthbound &quot;Lore of Violation&quot; for example allows the pseudo-deity to spend a point of faith to eat a mortal's soul for [successes on resisted roll between Earthbound's Wits + Occult and Target's Willpower, diff 8] points of faith(and other benefits).<br /> <br /> At an average of 0-2 points of faith per point spent, not very impressive right(ignoring possible difficulty modifiers and veneration rituals boosting the dicepool)? Now remember Master increases the number of targets by an order of magnitude per Extra faith spent, meaning said earthbound can spend 6 faith total to each 100,000 human souls(translating to between 100,000-200,000 faith in one go). If that earthbound has &quot;Lore of the Forge&quot; or &quot;Lore of Contamination&quot; 4, they can also spend 6 faith to simultaneously craft 100,000 artifacts to Hold all of that faith and transfer as necessary.<br /> <br /> For the earthquake in Los angelos: Los angelos takes up 501.55 square miles. This means that to effect all of it, the Earthbound needed to spend 2-3 extra faith on top of the normal expenditure and roll 3 successes on the extent of &quot;Lore of the Earth&quot; 5. I forget how long the quake lasted, but for the sake of the calc we'll say it was at least an hour, so the normal duration of the LotE 5 power lasting 1 round(equal to 1 minute) would require that the earthbound spend at least 2 faith(a 100x multiplier) to make it last 1 hour 40 minutes.<br /> <br /> That's 6 faith to cause the disaster in LA. Earthbound with any level in the &quot;hoard&quot; background(a requirement to Have a proper Reliquary) have 15+ maximum temporary faith regardless of their actual permanent faith score(and can get as high as 35 with enough investment in the background). With any kind of Cult and worship (a requirement for the earthbound to be active at all), they regain a minimum of 2 faith a month(with a maximum of 10 faith A Day with enough investments in the backgrounds). Reminder, the thing that attacked LA was an Archduke, It would be safe to assume it's backgrounds were either at their max or close to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-30-2022, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T15:44:57-07:00","id":1482413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482347#post1482347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side-note though:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not so simple. While the PLayer's Guide establishes this as default it also elaborates that this may also not be the case in the same section, and after that we have absolutely no concrete example of which path the lore follows. The question is open, and since the OP talks about the vampire making the Pact, the Fallen only matter <b><u>here</u></b> if assuming they can do it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I had forgotten to talk about the powers of the Earthbound, that the OP didn't seemed to understand since they have this exact feature: the ability to extend anything they do to Biblical Proportions. In addition to new Lores and more powerful Thralls, more worshipers and opportunities to extend their senses and so the reach of their Lore, they can increase the magnitude of said Lore to affect large areas for huge amounts of time, easily outdoing Elder levels of Disciplines for a fraction of the effort. A full power Earthbound (Faith 10, Mastery 5) spends far less XP on that than a Methuselah getting to 9 in a Discipline and can expand any power in area with a base radius of 10 yards (a very common thing) to a 5681.8 <b>miles</b> radius, which is enough to engulf the entirety of the Americas and then some, and this can be applied with equal ease to all their Lores.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482364#post1482364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesent that require a lot of faith though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;<i>a lot&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> We're talking three Backgrounds here, <b>Cult</b>, <b>Worship</b>, and <b>Mastery</b>. They're as hard to get as common Backgrounds goes, and Fallen can buy Backgrounds with XP like Mages. <b>Cult</b> defines how often the Earthbound get Faith, varying from 1/month to every day. <b>Worship</b> defines how much Faith you reap each time, which is double its rating. <b>Mastery</b> defines how many times you can extend a parameter of a Lore by a factor of 10 directly 1:1. Each such increase spends 1 temporary Faith.<br /> <br /> An Earthbound with each of those at 3, strong but nothing exceptional, gets 6 Faith every week and spends 3 to maximize a given parameter. That's enough to increase the area of a storm, for example, from 10 yards radius times Permanent Faith to almost 6 miles radius times Permanent Faith, which for an Earthbound can be easily 6 or more, so little less than a diameter of 72 miles. If the Lore itself requires Faith expenditure that would be 4, which is sensible, but still something this character can do reliably every week if they want to.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>Earthquake</b> uses successes to determine area, which isn't common, allocating 3 successes to it makes for an area of Permanent Faith in square miles, the above All 3 Then 6 Earthbound would be capable of covering an area of 6000 square miles, which seems about right for the coast of LA alone and more than enough to take the entire city (but only 1/6th of the Metro area). That's uncommon as an area definer and naturally makes for a smaller one than the usual radius base of most area-affecting Lore. An All Max Demon would be able to affect a 1,000,000 square miles area for 6 Faith that replenish completely every day, which is sufficient for almost a sixth of the entire Russian area, more than a fourth of the US, about 4/5th of India, and enough to be the 10th country in the world by Area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482370#post1482370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and the power level between Fallen and Earthbound isn't even on the same scale. A maxed out Earthbound is probably the strongest supernatural on Earth. I'd put &quot;the five&quot; above even the Antediluvians in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that it is viable for any Fallen to become an Earthbound. It isn't easy, and the personal cost usually isn't worth it, but it is doable for anyone really wanting to go that route.<br /> <br /> Contrary to Vampires, any Fallen has all the tools and potential they need to reach the apex of their power, you only need some effort and XP to realize it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482373#post1482373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget how long the quake lasted, but for the sake of the calc we'll say it was at least an hour, so the normal duration of the LotE 5 power lasting 1 round(equal to 1 minute) would require that the earthbound spend at least 2 faith(a 100x multiplier) to make it last 1 hour 40 minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unnecessary, IMO.<br /> <br /> The Devil's Night Earthquake is significant for its timing and magnitude, but not duration. None is given and it isn't referred as particularly long. Earthquakes usually last from 10 to 30 <i><b>seconds</b></i>, and even the longer ones rarely last more than 2 minutes. The release of energy in an Earthquake is just that big that it cause all that destruction in such a short time.<br /> <br /> With the <i>power</i> of <b>Earthquake</b> having a duration of 1 turn per Intensity, that's probably good enough for that event. I'd say probably no Faith whatsoever was used to increase it, specially considering that it had considerable Intensity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T21:32:54-07:00","id":1482459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482413#post1482413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unnecessary, IMO.<br /> <br /> The Devil's Night Earthquake is significant for its timing and magnitude, but not duration. None is given and it isn't referred as particularly long. Earthquakes usually last from 10 to 30 <i><b>seconds</b></i>, and even the longer ones rarely last more than 2 minutes. The release of energy in an Earthquake is just that big that it cause all that destruction in such a short time.<br /> <br /> With the <i>power</i> of <b>Earthquake</b> having a duration of 1 turn per Intensity, that's probably good enough for that event. I'd say probably no Faith whatsoever was used to increase it, specially considering that it had considerable Intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scary part is, nothing is Stopping an earthbound from doing that, since mastery applies to different aspects individually.<br /> <br /> If papa-archduke decided to go all in, they coul spend 5 extra faith to have their Death-quake effect most of the US, and then Another 5 faith on top of that to make it continuous for 69.444444... days(roughly 10 weeks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T05:36:49-07:00","id":1482483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482459#post1482459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scary part is, nothing is Stopping an earthbound from doing that, since mastery applies to different aspects individually.<br /> <br /> If papa-archduke decided to go all in, they coul spend 5 extra faith to have their Death-quake effect most of the US, and then Another 5 faith on top of that to make it continuous for 69.444444... days(roughly 10 weeks).</div> </div> </div> </div>And no &quot;Special Elder Level Disciplines&quot; needed, just a Background and a core book standard power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T07:53:23-07:00","id":1482490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482483#post1482483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no &quot;Special Elder Level Disciplines&quot; needed, just a Background and a core book standard power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I stand corrected, they are dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:56:38-07:00","id":1482502,"title":"","content":"My brother got the book for DtF and all I remember was this page of fluff text. The Demon had helped someone get to the top of a major corporation and the Man was telling him about a plan to deal with some corruption he became aware of. Then the Demon shocked the Man by telling him he couldn't do that; that the Demon wanted the corruption to collapse the company. When the Man asked why the &quot;Demon went through all this trouble,&quot; the Demon said none of it was any trouble for him; that he could crash the moon into the earth with &quot;a bit of trouble, for a second.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, flavor text and rules text are very different, but that page made it sound like Demons were pretty powerful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:42:57-07:00","id":1482531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482502#post1482502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, flavor text and rules text are very different, but that page made it sound like Demons were pretty powerful to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons are also liars, and that goes for both the Fallen and the other many entities in WoD that can be called &quot;demons&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is the thing the Vampire summoned really that powerful? It doesn't really matter at all. The thing will say it is, and it will have enough tricks to back it off. Are you going to challenge that? Being outright immune to mental control, messing with emotions and possession, plus resistant to illusions, is wonderful to <b>convince</b> the people that rely on such powers that you are stronger than them. And being able to come back from the dead as many times as needed, barring some very specific things you know your mark can't pull off, gives you a sense of security and a confidence that makes it all too easy to put a tough face.<br /> <br /> They don't believe in you, you just come back with another face, throw another pawn on them, and you can really scare those people. Just imagine the situation, an Elder Kindred face to face with a demon. The undead thinks they have complete control over the hapless &quot;victim&quot; until the entity inside starts to do whatever they want and state in no uncertain terms they're the one running the show. All their mental powers are useless against this thing, and it is completely fearless against life threats. While it isn't really immune to mundane persuasion, Torment means there's little the Vampire can threat it with that it didn't saw before. At most it says calmly and confidently that it won't fight back because it would just harm an asset for no gain, and this body is just an expendable vessel. &quot;Kill me if you want, enjoy your time, I'll come back, no hard feelings!&quot;<br /> <br /> When you come back from Hell possessing a new body, you approach the vampire with the same confidence, the same smile, and just starts with something like, &quot;expendable, see? A dime a dozen. Are you better to talk, now?&quot;<br /> <br /> Most Umbral entities can pull off something to that effect, the more dangerous can do that reliably. The Fallen folloe distinct rules because they're a Main Splat, but they're otherwise no exception to this: they're exceedingly powerful Umbral entities. Some are as powerful as the Infernalists think. None need to be to just be pretty convincing, and even if you don't believe, you simply have no recourse to prove them wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T17:38:41-07:00","id":1482868,"title":"","content":"I think that DtF suffer from that famous problem of being &quot;damn powerful&quot; in lore, but systematically damn weak. Any &quot;Joe the werewolf&quot; can turn most Demons into pieces, but demon sounds more scary lol<br /> <br /> I also feel the need to add that, in my opinion they have the least interesting set of powers in all WoD. I mean I can't remember a single interesting/cool/good/useful power from DtF. Also the setting just seems straight <i>boring.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T11:01:52-07:00","id":1482949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482868#post1482868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that DtF suffer from that famous problem of being &quot;damn powerful&quot; in lore, but systematically damn weak. Any &quot;Joe the werewolf&quot; can turn most Demons into pieces, but demon sounds more scary lol<br /> <br /> I also feel the need to add that, in my opinion they have the least interesting set of powers in all WoD. I mean I can't remember a single interesting/cool/good/useful power from DtF. Also the setting just seems straight <i>boring.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Demons aren't meant to be physically imposing if not geared towards that, while Garou are meant to be the most combat-wise powerful Main Splat. Combat isn't the only measure of power, and on top of that it is the measure Werewolves are intended to excel at.<br /> <br /> But the Demon is a possessing entity, and Werewolves don't have a lot of resources to deal with the entity itself. It isn't just a Bane and Gifts and Rituals meant to affect spirits don't have a clear mechanic for affecting Demons. Indeed, the lack of reference on them in the DtF's Storyteller's Companion indicates that they just don't affect the Fallen.<br /> <br /> So while a Werewolf is exceedingly capable to destroy the current body of a Demon, the Fallen are designed to take this as a setback, minor or major depending on some things, but nothing else. It is like saying that Werewolves are weak because any &quot;Jane the Vampire&quot; can affect the emotions of people better than most Werewolves, as they have the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> Now, it isn't to say that the powers of Demon don't need heavy revision. They definitely do. I'd still say there are some gems you're missing, like the entire Lore of Fundaments and the fact they're the only ones to have direct Life-Giving powers (not mere animation, but the ability to grant lasting life to objects or resurrecting others), with considerable ease at that, but outside those specific cases a lot of work must be done, and even them need a good mechanical polishing.<br /> <br /> On the setting being boring... I don't know, but the core book surely has a problem driving home what's there to see and do. The supplements are a must in this regard, with special consideration to <i>City of Angels</i>, <i>Damned and Deceived</i> and <i>Earthbound</i>. DnD here has special attention because, while it focus on Thralls, it has really, really good story pieces showcasing conflict with and also between Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T18:23:46-07:00","id":1482999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons aren't meant to be physically imposing if not geared towards that, while Garou are meant to be the most combat-wise powerful Main Splat. Combat isn't the only measure of power, and on top of that it is the measure Werewolves are intended to excel at.<br /> <br /> But the Demon is a possessing entity, and Werewolves don't have a lot of resources to deal with the entity itself. It isn't just a Bane and Gifts and Rituals meant to affect spirits don't have a clear mechanic for affecting Demons. Indeed, the lack of reference on them in the DtF's Storyteller's Companion indicates that they just don't affect the Fallen.<br /> <br /> So while a Werewolf is exceedingly capable to destroy the current body of a Demon, the Fallen are designed to take this as a setback, minor or major depending on some things, but nothing else. It is like saying that Werewolves are weak because any &quot;Jane the Vampire&quot; can affect the emotions of people better than most Werewolves, as they have the Blood Bond. </div> </div> </div>Well, with all due respect, this is just a way to avoid facing the question/problem, ignoring the elephant in the room, so to speak, it's just like saying &quot;vampires are too busy ruling the world to care about werewolves&quot;. Balancing issues apart, the thing IMO is that Demons just don't &quot;stand out&quot; in any significant way and are basically outclassed by other splats in everything they're able to do, for me, they always felt a bit &quot;off&quot;. But, I'm far from an expert in DtF, this is just my impression anyway.<br /> <br /> Btw I loved the &quot;Jane the Vampire&quot; hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T21:46:48-07:00","id":1483011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1482999#post1482999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with all due respect, this is just a way to avoid facing the question/problem, ignoring the elephant in the room, so to speak, it's just like saying &quot;vampires are too busy ruling the world to care about werewolves&quot;. Balancing issues apart, the thing IMO is that Demons just don't &quot;stand out&quot; in any significant way and are basically outclassed by other splats in everything they're able to do, for me, they always felt a bit &quot;off&quot;. But, I'm far from an expert in DtF, this is just my impression anyway.<br /> <br /> Btw I loved the &quot;Jane the Vampire&quot; hahaha</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to avoid anything, your argument was built comparing the most combat oriented splat to another and saying the other doesn't stand because it can't stand in combat. This can be said of every single other splat, because Werewolf is still the most combat oriented splat.<br /> <br /> If you want to see where it stand out, you have to look elsewhere, because every splat stands out at something different. Demon stand out in how easy it is for them to figure out things, tempt people and mess with others with impunity. That's why I usually talk about the innate abilities of immunity to mind control and the ease to come back from Hell, because those are key to play with confidence against anything others can throw on you. Pacts let you offer benefits in a very versatile way, both to give what they want and to empower Thralls as you wish, and the option of scourging your Thralls is another very powerful weapon.<br /> <br /> All that together, Fallen really stand out as negotiators. It is hard to fool them and they have no reason to tell the truth, they can offer anything you desire or just mess with you without ever fearing reprisal, and while others have a great need for secrecy they can reap Faith by showing off. Their powers on top of that do have a recurring theme of Truth, of messing with reality by reaching its actual workings, of playing the tools that crafted reality to begin with, but here is where the set is messily written. Yet, the themes are there.<br /> <br /> You may not see any appeal on anything of this. No problem. I find it lots of fun to roleplay a Fallen either as a PC or NPC, but that's me. It isn't like playing other lines, each fun on their own ways. I've played and ST'd Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling and Demon and I loved each one in a different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T22:31:01-07:00","id":1483017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not trying to avoid anything, your argument was built comparing the most combat oriented splat to another and saying the other doesn't stand because it can't stand in combat. This can be said of every single other splat, because Werewolf is still the most combat oriented splat. </div> </div> </div>Well, I think I didn't express myself very well, I only meant that people would usually think &quot;Heck! Don't mess with him, he's a demon!&quot; in a way to show that culturally, we are more or less inclined to fear a demon much more than a werewolf. Like the word in itself carry a stronger semantic load (or stronger connotation, if you prefer), so to speak, but then the guy's going to change his mind when he sees that a werewolf is clearly superior to a demon in any physical confrontation in WoD (unlike in basically any other RPG). That's just what I meant, not that it matters that much to the Fallen's relevance. Their relevance is another topic, that I expressed in a very personal way, I simply fail to see all the appeal playing with a Fallen has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T11:32:30-07:00","id":1483056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482292-demons-in-vtm-lore-vs-demons-in-dtf-lore?p=1483017#post1483017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only meant that people would usually think &quot;Heck! Don't mess with him, he's a demon!&quot; in a way to show that culturally, we are more or less inclined to fear a demon much more than a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that, but then we have a more nuanced situation here.<br /> <br /> First, again, Werewolf is the most combat-oriented splat, so there aren't much we can do about that. Making any splat more fearsome in physical confrontation would defeat their purpose in the setting. Also considering that Garou are also more than what a werewolf is in most settings, they have a far greater and more complex role in WoD. All in all making the Fallen clearly superior wasn't an option from the design perspective.<br /> <br /> Other RPGs don't necessarily make it so simple, either. D&amp;D comes to mind (obviously) and Fiends there run the whole gamut of power, most being clearly below the standard werewolf. You don't fear them because they're all individually strong, you fear them because of all the connotations they bring with them.<br /> <br /> Here again, not that you have to personally be impressed, but the idea is that the Fallen are to be feared by what they can bring in a greater scale. From a Werewolf perspective, for example, this is a foe that can patiently work towards their corruption while they can do little beyond causing it minor setbacks. Death for a well prepared Fallen just means an XP tax to recover Faith and Torment, and other splats won't know even that cost. The Fallen is an opponent that has infinite time in their hands and the stakes are cosmic, the fate of your immortal soul just the least important, and you simply can't win in their game through physical confrontation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}